{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-72492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-72492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${c}_{22}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is **not** in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-72492" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6f4718e5f62c2db3fa117f08a0f1728eb0ea3c554eae9144e2ad52fb1b40444"} {"question" "q-72492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-72492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A$ only"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"] ["text" "$C$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-72492" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$C$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-73149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-73149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{31}$ and ${a}_{42}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-73149" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6f4718e5f62c2db3fa117f08a0f1728eb0ea3c554eae9144e2ad52fb1b40444"} {"question" "q-73149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-73149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${a}_{21}$ and ${a}_{31}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{31}$ and ${a}_{34}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{31}$ and ${a}_{42}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{31}$ only"] ["text" "${a}_{42}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-73149" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${a}_{31}$ and ${a}_{42}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-129217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-129217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the leading entry ${a}_{45}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-129217" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6f4718e5f62c2db3fa117f08a0f1728eb0ea3c554eae9144e2ad52fb1b40444"} {"question" "q-129217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-129217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$A$ and $B$ only"] ["text" "$A$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$"] ["text" "$B$ and $C$ only"] ["text" "$B$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-129217" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$B$ and $C$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-129233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-129233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is **not** in row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a37687484f1fef3483f7fe51d74240b0a9e89421c0af"} {"question" "q-129233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f6f4718e5f62c2db3fa117f08a0f1728eb0ea3c554eae9144e2ad52fb1b40444"} {"question" "q-129233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14084523/state.json" "file_sha256" "5cd604a8469db0d9bcc6a3768